-- title:
--   Formally smooth local algebras: Ω_{S/A} free on dt
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ and $S$ be commutative local rings and let $i : A \to S$ be a ring homomorphism which is formally smooth and essentially of finite type. Assume that the composite of $i$ with the residue map $S \to \kappa(S)$ is surjective, i.e. every element of the residue field of $S$ is the class of $i(a)$ for some $a \in A$. Let $t \in S$ be an element such that the maximal ideal of $S$ is the sum of the ideal $(\mathfrak m_A)S$ generated by the image of the maximal ideal of $A$ under $i$ and the principal ideal $(t)$, and such that $t \notin (\mathfrak m_A)S$. Then, giving $S$ the $A$-algebra structure induced by $i$, for every $\omega$ in the module of Kähler differentials $\Omega_{S/A}$ there is exactly one $s \in S$ with $\omega = s\,\mathrm{d}t$. Equivalently, $\mathrm{d}t$ is a basis of $\Omega_{S/A}$ over $S$, so $\Omega_{S/A}$ is free of rank one on $\mathrm{d}t$. No noetherian, domain or valuation hypothesis is imposed on $A$ or $S$.
--
--   This is the local form of the statement that a formally smooth morphism whose closed fibre has maximal ideal generated by one element has free differential module of rank one, with $\mathrm{d}t$ as generator; the base is an arbitrary local ring, which covers the cases of a field, a discrete valuation ring and a general (possibly non-discrete) valuation ring. It is used to produce a local parameter with prescribed differential in [`AlgebraicCurve.exists_section_localRing_apply_eq_of_ord_eq_one_of_mem_smoothLocus`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.exists_section_localRing_apply_eq_of_ord_eq_one_of_mem_smoothLocus).
